    breadcrumbName: "Email & Funnels",
    bodyHtml: "<h2>The Funnel Build Doesn&#x27;t Have to Be Yours</h2>\n<p>One of my coaches told me that if I was doing work I could pay someone else to do, I was stealing from my own company. I was like, whoa.</p>\n<p>So here&#x27;s my question for you. Is there a funnel build or an email campaign you&#x27;re still doing yourself?</p>\n<p>That&#x27;s the work this page is about. You send the task. The same team builds the funnel, sets up the sequence, and sends the campaign. You bring the words, and we do the build.</p>\n<p>We don&#x27;t call this outsourcing. Our word for it is insourcing. Picture the people who build your funnels and send your emails all coming into one office, with a team leader on the floor every day. That&#x27;s how we work.</p>\n<!--BOOK_A_CALL-->\n<h2>What the Team Builds and Sends</h2>\n<p>Here&#x27;s the email and funnel work you can hand off.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Email campaign builds and sends: newsletters, promotions and broadcasts</li>\n<li>Automation sequences: welcome series, drip campaigns and lead nurture</li>\n<li>GoHighLevel funnel and workflow builds</li>\n<li>Landing page design and development</li>\n<li>A/B testing setup and management</li>\n<li>Klaviyo, ActiveCampaign and Mailchimp builds</li>\n<li>Segmentation</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The team works in tools such as GoHighLevel, Klaviyo, ActiveCampaign and Mailchimp. We plug into your existing tech stack.</p>\n<p>Now the part I&#x27;d rather tell you up front. The plan covers the build. The words need to come from you or your copywriter.</p>\n<p>We don&#x27;t manage ad spend. The team does make ad graphics and ad video cuts.</p>\n<p>White label work is on all plans. Our page on <a href=\"/services/white-label/marketing\">white label marketing help</a> shows how the team builds this under your brand.</p>\n<p>If your funnel needs CRM setup and pipelines behind it, that work is on our <a href=\"/services/crm-automation\">CRM and automation page</a>. Not sure what else you could send? <a href=\"/blog/tasks-a-team-can-take-off-your-plate\">See everything the team can do</a>.</p>\n<h2>How a Funnel Gets From Your Head to Done</h2>\n<p>You drop a task into our request form or send an email. Write it out, record a Loom video, attach a doc, or send a quick voice note. It can be as short as &quot;Build this GoHighLevel workflow.&quot;</p>\n<p>That&#x27;s where your North American account manager comes in. They assign the right specialist, manage the timeline, and check the work before you see it. Your account manager speaks fluent English and bridges any language gaps with the production team.</p>\n<p>Then you review it and ask for changes. Revisions are unlimited on every plan. After that, the next task starts. Most tasks ship in 1 to 3 business days.</p>\n<p>A full funnel is a bigger project. So we break it into tasks and do them in order: the landing page, the sequence, the integrations.</p>\n<p>The team works together in one office with backup power and more than one internet connection, so an outage doesn&#x27;t stop your work. No excuses. Your work gets around-the-clock attention.</p>\n<p>Every plan comes with a North American account manager, a team leader, 2 developers, 2 technical Virtual Assistants, 2 designers, and me on 2 weekly group calls. And you work with the same people every month, so they learn your brand, your preferences, and your standards.</p>\n<p>You can see every step on our <a href=\"/how-it-works\">How It Works</a> page.</p>\n<h2>Zach&#x27;s Agency Sold the Funnels. One of Our Teams Built Them.</h2>\n<p>Zach runs a marketing agency called Convert on Command. His agency sold done-for-you funnels, and Zach was doing all the fulfillment by himself.</p>\n<p>He handed his production work to one of our teams and got 16 hours a week back. With that additional time he was able to add $160,000 a month selling his high-ticket offer.</p>\n<p>What did he hand off? His case study lists it in his own words: “creating the funnels, simple video edits, websites, integrations, emails campaign, and anything that is techy and outside our knowledge base.”</p>\n<p>His full story is on the site, under the title “<a href=\"/case-studies/freed-up-16-hours-a-week-added-160k-a-month-to-their-bottom-line\">Freed Up 16 Hours A Week &amp; Added $160k A Month To Their Bottom Line</a>”. That&#x27;s what DeskTeam360 is all about.</p>\n<h2>Funnels and Email Are on Every Plan</h2>\n<p>Every plan covers every service. The only difference is how many tasks run at once.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Entrepreneur: $1,497 a month, 1 task at a time</li>\n<li>Marketer: $2,994 a month, 2 tasks at a time</li>\n<li>Agency: $4,491 a month, 3 tasks at a time</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There are no contracts. It&#x27;s month to month, and you can cancel any time. There&#x27;s a 30-day money-back guarantee.</p>\n<p>It&#x27;s a full refund within the first 30 days, with no conditions. One more number for you: $2.5 million processed, zero chargebacks.</p>\n<p>See the <a href=\"/#pricing\">plans</a>, from $1,497 a month.</p>",
